    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into the July 2nd slate with high expectations for our top-tier outfielders, as **Kyle Tucker** (78.10) and **Andy Pages** (70.62) represent our most potent scoring options against Randy V\u00e1squez. Both benefit significantly from a favorable SP_xERA of 4.76 and strong lineup positioning, providing the ideal platform for R and RBI production. **Jackson Merrill** (68.44) and **Cole Carrigg** (67.90) also present elite efficiency, with **Carrigg** taking advantage of a park factor boost (+14%) and **Merrill** maintaining high upside against Roki Sasaki due to a combination of speed-driven metrics and a beneficial matchup. **Sam Antonacci** (60.82) rounds out our strongest plays, leveraging a leadoff spot and a +10% SP skill adjustment to solidify our offensive floor.\n\nOur most difficult personnel decision centered on **Nolan Schanuel** (42.11), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While **Schanuel** carries a respectable projection, the decision to bench him was ultimately driven by his unfavorable matchup against Bryce Miller (2.42 xERA) and the optimizer\u2019s preference for the higher-upside profiles of **Josh Lowe** and **Dominic Smith**, who possess more favorable park and platoon contexts despite the presence of an elite arm. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Josh Lowe** and the other players listed as \"Lineup Pending\"; should official lineups shift those bats into the bottom third of the order, we may need to pivot. Furthermore, while we monitor the health of **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL, our current configuration relies heavily on the aggressive base-running profiles of **Miguel Vargas** and **Cole Carrigg** to capitalize on catchers with poor pop times, keeping our stolen base category competitiveness intact.",
